{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"reveries@example.com","session":"opencode:rvr-018","created_at":"2026-10-03T23:38:26.378Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"Issue #18 required a redaction, secrets, and confidential-evidence policy, and the open implementation covered only part of it.","decision":"Refuse likely credentials before a note write and again at every transport boundary, hide soft-redacted records from delivery, carry confidential rationale as an opaque vault:v1 pointer that requires a record-domain signature, and add deliberate hard-redaction tooling that rewrites notes into a root commit behind a genesis discontinuity checkpoint and reports per-remote follow-up work.","impact":"Secret-bearing evidence can no longer be published through Reveries, automatic delivery cannot surface soft-redacted or pointer-bearing records, and hard redaction is auditable without claiming deletion outside the repository.","recurrence_control":"Boundary tests assert that publication, receive, and sync refuse detected secrets, that pointer publication requires a signature, and that hard redaction severs known local copies while naming remote work.","alternatives":["Rely on documentation alone and scan only at publication, which leaves a secret in local notes and allows local commits to hold it","Treat hard redaction as deletion, which cannot be honored across clones and mirrors"],"sources":[{"relation":"requested-by","kind":"issue","ref":"github:phynics/reveries#18"}],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
